From 38fafd05c472dff58ecf07e1ad277d975478c66a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 00:28:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] clk: mediatek: mt8173: fix the FHCTL DDS mask width

MT8173's PLLs carry pcwbits = 21, so the frequency hopping controller's DDS
field is bits 20:0. The FH() macro declares .dds_mask = GENMASK(21, 0),
which is one bit too wide; it was copied from the other SoCs in this
family, whose PLLs really do have a 22-bit field. MediaTek's own MT8173
FHCTL driver masks with 0x1FFFFF throughout (MASK21b in mt_freqhopping.c).

The extra bit is not merely cosmetic. hopping_hw_flow() polls

	readl_poll_timeout_atomic(regs->reg_mon, mon_dds,
				  (mon_dds & dds_mask) == new_dds, 10, 1000);

and new_dds comes from mtk_pll_calc_values(), i.e. it is always a 21-bit
value. On this hardware FHCTL_MON has bit 21 set, so with the wider mask
the comparison can never be true: measured on an MT8173 board (Amazon Fire
HD 10 2017) the MON register reads 0x00370000 for a target of 0x170000.
Every hop therefore ran to the full timeout and logged "FHCTL hopping
timeout", even though the PLL had reached the requested frequency in about
31 us.

The same mask then feeds the write-back

	con_pcw_tmp = (con_pcw_tmp | (readl(regs->reg_mon) & dds_mask) |
		       data->pcwchg);

so it would also have put bit 21 of MON into a CON1 field that does not
belong to pcw.

Only mt8173 is changed. The other users of this macro (mt6795, mt8186,
mt8192, mt8195) have 22-bit pcw fields and are left alone.

Fixes: 45a5cbe05d1f ("clk: mediatek: mt8173: Add support for frequency hopping through FHCTL")
Signed-off-by: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt8173-apmixedsys.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt8173-apmixedsys.c b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt8173-apmixedsys.c
index d7d416172..327240cd3 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt8173-apmixedsys.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt8173-apmixedsys.c
@@ -100,7 +100,7 @@ enum fh_pll_id {
 			.fh_id = _fhid,					\
 			.fh_ver = FHCTL_PLLFH_V1,			\
 			.fhx_offset = _offset,				\
-			.dds_mask = GENMASK(21, 0),			\
+			.dds_mask = GENMASK(20, 0),			\
 			.slope0_value = 0x6003c97,			\
 			.slope1_value = 0x6003c97,			\
 			.sfstrx_en = BIT(2),				\
